  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> be a non-negative integer. Then the number of divisors of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;of the number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>11</mn></mfenced><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>13</mn></mfenced><mn>13</mn></msup></math> is equal to _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "924",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>11</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>13</mn><mn>13</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now, power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> must be zero,</p><p>Power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> can be anything,</p><p>Power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math> can be anything.</p><p>But, power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> should be even.</p><p>So, required number of divisors is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>924</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
